#! ia 1.0

@kind governance
  meaning
    says "A standing 'ought' — a norm that always holds (law · principle · convention)."
    answers "Is this record a standing norm that always holds, rather than a permission or routing rule?"
  data
    order 0
    lane authority

@kind contract
  meaning
    says "An obligation that another record relies on: a structural body schema or a signature between parties. The schema and contract discriminators have distinct dialects under this shared kind."
    answers "Does this record pin a structure that something else relies on?"
  data
    order 1
    lane contracts
    authority-lane authority

@kind definition
  meaning
    says "The meaning of a term or the membership of an axis (concept · boundary · method · taxonomy member)."
    answers "Does this record say what a term, boundary, method or domain member means?"
  data
    order 2
    lane definitions

@kind template
  meaning
    says "A reusable output shape. An implemented consumer is required to instantiate it into records or files."
    answers "Is this record a reusable output shape that a consumer instantiates?"
  data
    order 3
    lane templates

@kind check
  meaning
    says "A declared evaluation gate. Its bound evaluator produces a verdict; the declaration alone does not execute."
    answers "Does this record declare a gate whose bound evaluator yields a verdict?"
  data
    order 4
    lane enforcement

@kind policy
  meaning
    says "An access or routing rule — who may, and what flows where."
    answers "Does this record declare who may act or where something flows?"
  data
    order 5
    lane enforcement

@kind binding
  meaning
    says "An explicit connection between an actor, invocation or trigger and behavior. A host consumer supplies execution."
    answers "Does this record wire an actor or trigger to behavior a host executes?"
  data
    order 6
    lane bindings

